ation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"39a5044860d51535de95c80025ce4659e514237b86c87c63506b60e9a943224a","event_uuid":"8a6c94c6-2145-4620-9e22-f7fa0e0288ce","position":{"commit_sha":"402975ac31c1fca7e544d97f1477a7e042503254","position":"1787092068823713001-8a6c94c6-2145-4620-9e22-f7fa0e0288ce"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d29b947b3b60a8bb72cde79c2a0dca95aae6c7b37fc267874c7e9f6186af5287","event_uuid":"5dee8acb-895e-433c-8780-0983208bdb09","position":{"commit_sha":"29df8a005603ee7c849d646078f5b11d6091b948","position":"1787092073725500001-5dee8acb-895e-433c-8780-0983208bdb09"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed a two-part incomplete implementation in the handwritten MCP adapter. E1 built the real server and inspected both the registered callable and live FastMCP schema in the same process: signature `(id1, id2)` and schema properties `{id1,id2}` both omitted `relation`, ruling out stale client/server cache. E2 drove a real MCP unlink against an ephemeral pair holding `blocks` then `relates_to`: the runtime spy recorded exactly two positional arguments, MCP removed the newest `relates_to` edge, while the library control `rebar.unlink(a,b,\"blocks\")` removed only `blocks`. E3 temporarily added only the optional callable parameter while deliberately leaving the two-argument delegate unchanged: the live schema then accepted `relation=\"blocks\"`, but the spy still recorded only `(a,b)` and MCP still removed `relates_to`; instrumentation was removed and the worktree is clean.\n\nRoot cause: `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets` independently omits the already-supported optional relation selector from both its registered signature and its `rebar.unlink` call. Both omissions are necessary to explain the inability to express the selector and the pair-scoped fallback at runtime. Defect legitimacy is `incomplete-implementation`: the signed final ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish requires zero intended write-parameter divergences and total lib/CLI/MCP parity; relation-scoped unlink is already authoritative in docs/user-guide.md, docs/cli-reference.md, core/library code, and tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py. The older ticket-model prose and commit 73abb580 only record the earlier change scope, not a permanent divergence. Expected behavior: an explicit MCP relation removes exactly that edge; omission preserves pair-scoped most-recent behavior.","timestamp":1787087293004668001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report.\n\nProblem — MCP unlink_tickets could not select a relation when one ticket pair held multiple active relations.\n\nProven root cause — the handwritten adapter in src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py omitted the already-supported optional selector from both its registered FastMCP signature and its rebar.unlink delegate.\n\nProof — the real server schema exposed only id1/id2; a runtime spy showed a real MCP call forwarded exactly two args and removed newer relates_to; the library control removed explicit blocks. A signature-only experiment made FastMCP accept relation but the unchanged delegate still removed relates_to, independently proving value loss.\n\nTest — tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py was collected and legitimately RED before repair because the live schema lacked relation. Held out from the fixer, it became GREEN (2 passed). Restoring the full original signature/delegate omission returned the explicit case to RED at the schema assertion; restoring only the delegate omission returned it to RED at the persisted relation set. Restoring the repair returned 2 GREEN. A formatting-only structural refactor left the oracle GREEN, proving it asserts behavior rather than implementation shape.\n\nFix — unlink_tickets now declares relation: str | None = None, forwards it unchanged, and documents explicit versus omitted behavior. docs/mcp-reference.md was regenerated from the registered tool contract.\n\nScope and safety — callers already converge on the proven public library/core contract; no behavioral dependency on the unreachable selector exists. No dependency was added, no existing test weakened, and omitted relation still removes the most-recent edge. Focused live-MCP/library/CLI/reference matrix: 70 passed; MCP reference drift, make lint, make typecheck, and git diff --check pass.\n\nParity census — rule: unlink must accept an optional relation selector and remove exactly that edge when supplied. CLI: src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py::unlink_cli/unlink_core accepts it. MCP/API: fixed at src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets. Public library: src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py::unlink accepts/forwards it. Automated callers: reconciler apply_inbound_records.py already supplies relation explicitly through the public library. Dual-direction mirror: link already requires relation; relates_to reciprocal removal is performed by unlink_core and preserved by the held-out oracle.\n\nSiblings — no second code adapter omission exists for unlink. The maintained ticket-model and packaged CLI overview still state the pre-change no-relation contract; filed and linked asbestos-lithe-kouprey rather than expanding this code repair.\n\nResidual risk and prevention — ticketed documentation drift as asbestos-lithe-kouprey. No other observed fragility remains undispositioned.\n\nReplication — the original real-MCP double-edge scenario now removes explicit blocks while preserving relates_to and its reciprocal; omitting the selector removes newer relates_to and leaves blocks.","timestamp":1787089445348566001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] External Gerrit gates satisfied before merge and close. Gerrit change 1873 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1873), patch set 1 revision 9ba561da85fb744896f760a5a4a513499cd36431: LLM-Review +1; Verified +1; zero unresolved comments; submittable true. GitHub Actions run 32189359725 completed success with all gating jobs green: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32189359725. Gerrit Rebase-If-Necessary submitted the change to main as authoritative merged SHA 07320e7649ee50e16279e34ed666f5bf35b5d8cb on 2026-08-18 22:15 UTC; gerrit/main contains that commit.","timestamp":1787091325688337001}],"created_at":1787086578886175001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0639fd5b-bf48-4273-b1cb-c9f445abff5b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1128-505b-54ac-497f"},{"link_uuid":"c5b18e09-31a9-41f5-8272-bad6fd03b606","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2f8f-7488-3f43-4414"}],"description":"## Context\nThe public CLI and Python library support relation-specific unlink so callers can remove exactly one edge when the same ticket pair carries multiple relations. The registered MCP `unlink_tickets` tool accepts only `id1` and `id2` and delegates `rebar.unlink` without `relation`. FastMCP therefore advertises no relation field and execution takes the pair-scoped fallback, removing the most-recent edge rather than the requested edge.\n\nThe signed final write-surface ruling on `restoring-shallow-blobfish` requires total parameter parity across library, CLI, and MCP with zero intended divergences. The earlier relation-scoped change explicitly left MCP outside that change scope, but did not establish a permanent divergence.\n\n## Proven root cause\n`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets` independently omits the already-supported optional relation selector from (1) its registered callable signature/live FastMCP schema and (2) its `rebar.unlink` delegate call. Runtime experiments proved both omissions: current MCP forwards only two args and removes the newest relation; a signature-only mutation makes the schema accept `relation` but still loses the value at the delegate.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Add `relation: str | None = None` to the MCP callable, matching the public library contract.\n- Forward `relation` unchanged to `rebar.unlink`.\n- Update the tool description to document explicit relation-scoped removal and the omitted-selector fallback.\n- Regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md` from the registered tool contract with `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`.\n- Add a held-out interface oracle through the real FastMCP registration and real ephemeral ticket store.\n- Preserve pair-scoped most-recent behavior when `relation` is omitted.\n- Complete the five-slot write-surface parity census required by rebar-debug. Repair in this ticket only an identical missing-parameter/missing-forwarding omission on the same unlink operation; file and `discovered_from`-link a separate bug for any different operation, broader behavioral mismatch, or design-dependent gap.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: signed total write-parameter parity ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish plus relation-scoped unlink contract in docs/user-guide.md, docs/cli-reference.md, and test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py.\n- trigger_preconditions: one ordered ticket pair holds `blocks` then `relates_to`; MCP receives `relation=\"blocks\"`.\n- production_path: real FastMCP registration/schema -> `unlink_tickets` -> public `rebar.unlink` -> real git-backed ticket store.\n- test_tier: interface/lifecycle test; a unit test cannot prove live schema binding and persisted edge selection together.\n- observable_postcondition: live schema advertises optional relation; explicit `blocks` removes only blocks and leaves relates_to; omitted relation removes newest relates_to and leaves blocks.\n- negative_control: omit relation and verify the existing pair-scoped fallback is unchanged.\n- collateral_invariants: the unselected edge and reciprocal relation state remain correct.\n- ci_gate: focused interface suite, `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check`, make lint, and make typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] MCP unlink_tickets accepts an optional `relation` parameter.\n- [x] The live MCP schema advertises `relation` as optional with the same string-or-null type as the library contract.\n- [x] A supplied relation is forwarded unchanged.\n- [x] Supplying `blocks` removes only that edge while preserving `relates_to`.\n- [x] Omitting relation preserves the documented pair-scoped most-recent fallback.\n- [x] The selected interface test is collected and executes without skip/xfail.\n- [x] The selected interface test returns to RED when the signature omission is restored.\n- [x] The selected interface test returns to RED when the forwarding omission is restored.\n- [x] The five-slot parity census records a cited result and disposition for every surface.\n- [x] Every confirmed sibling outside the identical unlink-adapter omission is recorded as a separately linked bug.\n- [x] Focused MCP/link tests pass.\n- [x] The generated MCP reference drift check passes.\n- [x] make lint passes.\n- [x] make typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"expose, document, and forward optional relation on MCP unlink_tickets"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py","reason":"held-out live-schema and persisted relation-selection RED/GREEN oracle"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"regenerate the public MCP tool contract from the updated docstring and schema"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2f8f-7488-3f43-4414"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8a6c94c6-2145-4620-9e22-f7fa0e0288ce","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["mcp","parity","links"],"ticket_id":"88b9-c847-3a2e-4c63","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP unlink_tickets cannot target a specific relation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["37edabb5-78e7-4da9-84c1-3b477f606e55","46b9a6b7-6e36-480f-a185-618c3c130185","6ec0bfc9-7411-4c16-bdb4-55443a0a6313","8d021c10-172f-4a32-a749-7028be6220af","6cc74c19-5a6f-45c3-946b-74f79a4f5e7f","07d86d8b-f09a-445d-b999-e22f040a7a4c","c5b18e09-31a9-41f5-8272-bad6fd03b606","53d0fc3a-d4e7-4b9f-8e60-e30e6281f4e7","15851148-adfb-4a75-b78d-4ba272e886fe","8a6c94c6-2145-4620-9e22-f7fa0e0288ce","5dee8acb-895e-433c-8780-0983208bdb09"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787094859249387001,"uuid":"3e2d1435-32d2-4550-a4c1-e31def881a12"}